    <ShortLegislativeSummaryEn>A legislative summary is currently being prepared for this bill by the Parliamentary Information and Research Service of the Library of Parliament. Meanwhile, the following executive summary is available. 

On 17 June 2009, the Minister of Citizenship and Immigration introduced Bill C-45, An Act to amend the Immigration and Refugee Protection Act, in the House of Commons and it was given first reading.

Clause 1 of Bill C-45 amends the objectives of the Immigration and Refugee Protection Act with respect to immigration to add the word "public" to the reference to the protection of health and safety currently specified in section 3(1)(h) of the Act. The amended Act will, in the context of immigration, aim to protect public health and safety and to maintain the security of Canadian society.

Clauses 2 and 3 of Bill C-45 amend the Immigration and Refugee Protection Act to allow immigration officers to refuse to authorize foreign nationals to work in Canada if they are deemed to be at risk of exploitation.</ShortLegislativeSummaryEn>
    <ShortLegislativeSummaryFr>Le Service d'information et de recherche parlementaires de la Bibliothèque du Parlement rédige actuellement le résumé législatif de ce projet de loi. Entre-temps, il met à votre disposition le sommaire suivant. 

Le 17 juin 2009, Le ministre de la Citoyenneté et de l'immigration a déposé le projet de loi C-45, Loi modifiant la Loi sur l'immigration et la protection des réfugiés, à la Chambre des communes en première lecture.

L'article premier du projet de loi modifie les objectifs de la La Loi sur l'immigration et la protection des réfugiés (LIPR) en matière d'immigration afin d'ajouter le terme « publiques » au libellé relatif à la protection de la santé et de la sécurité de l'actuel alinéa 3(1)h) de la LIPR.  Une fois modifiée, la LIPR aura pour objet, dans le contexte de l'immigration, de protéger la santé et la sécurité publiques et de garantir la sécurité de la société canadienne.

Les articles 2 et 3 du projet de loi C-45 modifient la LIPR afin de permettre à un agent d'immigration de refuser d'autoriser un étranger à exercer un emploi au Canada s'il estime qu'il y a risque d'exploitation.</ShortLegislativeSummaryFr>
    <ShortLegislativeSummary>A legislative summary is currently being prepared for this bill by the Parliamentary Information and Research Service of the Library of Parliament. Meanwhile, the following executive summary is available. 

On 17 June 2009, the Minister of Citizenship and Immigration introduced Bill C-45, An Act to amend the Immigration and Refugee Protection Act, in the House of Commons and it was given first reading.

Clause 1 of Bill C-45 amends the objectives of the Immigration and Refugee Protection Act with respect to immigration to add the word "public" to the reference to the protection of health and safety currently specified in section 3(1)(h) of the Act. The amended Act will, in the context of immigration, aim to protect public health and safety and to maintain the security of Canadian society.

Clauses 2 and 3 of Bill C-45 amend the Immigration and Refugee Protection Act to allow immigration officers to refuse to authorize foreign nationals to work in Canada if they are deemed to be at risk of exploitation.</ShortLegislativeSummary>
